The class `SingleMaterialize` is a thin delegating operator that merely forwards subscription to the source `Single` and wraps the observer with `MaterializeSingleObserver`. It contains no computational logic, state changes, or loops whose performance characteristics would vary meaningfully. Benchmarking such a trivial pass‑through would not provide useful insight, and any measured overhead would be dominated by the underlying RxJava infrastructure rather than this class itself. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark for this code is unnecessary.